FILE: THIRD_PARTY.md [1-260]
    1: # Third-party software distributed with iolbox
    2: 
    3: iolbox bundles the following third-party components. Their licenses are their
    4: own; this file records what we ship, from where, pinned to an exact version and
    5: checksum, and how we comply with each license.
    6: 
    7: ---
    8: 
    9: ## Apple Silicon macOS archive
   10: 
   11: The `iolbox-macos-arm64.tar.gz` archive contains the Go `iolbox` launcher,
   12: **two** Linux payloads produced by `runtime/pack-native.sh` ƒ?" one linux/amd64
   13: and one linux/arm64 ƒ?" the locked Lima profile/provisioner files, and this
   14: notice. It contains no guest disk, hypervisor, Lima installation, or Cisco
   15: software.
   16: 
   17: The launcher selects one payload from the profile it resolves: the
   18: linux/arm64 payload for the `native-arm64` profile, the linux/amd64 payload
   19: (run under Rosetta) for the `debian13`/`jammy`/`debian12` profiles.
   20: 
   21: ### Separately installed and fetched components
   22: 
   23: - Lima is an Apache-2.0 licensed, user-installed prerequisite. iolbox neither
   24:   redistributes nor installs, upgrades, or removes Lima.
   25: - Lima downloads the digest-locked Debian 13/trixie default, Debian 13/trixie
   26:   native-arm64, or Ubuntu 22.04/Jammy compatibility guest image. The guest
   27:   image, apt package indexes, and guest packages are fetched at provisioning
   28:   time and are not embedded in the archive.
   29: - Users supply any legally held IOL/IOU image. iolbox does not distribute or
   30:   depend on Cisco software. **x86_64 IOL is the only supported IOL
   31:   architecture on every profile in this archive**; i386/i86bi and
   32:   arm64-native IOL are unsupported. On the Rosetta profiles x86_64 IOL is
   33:   translated by Apple's Rosetta; on `native-arm64` it is translated by
   34:   qemu-user inside the guest (see the QEMU boundary note below).
   35: 
   36: ### VPCS binary redistributed inside the payloads
   37: 
   38: `runtime/fetch-vpcs.sh` checks out the GNS3 VPCS project at the immutable
   39: `v0.8.3` ref (release commit `3870ae8`) and builds it; `runtime/pack-native.sh`
   40: places the resulting binary at `bin/vpcs` in the payload. Both payloads are
   41: built from that same pinned ref ƒ?" the linux/amd64 binary natively on the
   42: builder, the linux/arm64 binary with `aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc` via
   43: `fetch-vpcs.sh --arch arm64`. The upstream project is BSD-2-Clause licensed:
   44: 
   45: - Source repository: <https://github.com/GNS3/vpcs>
   46: - Pinned source archive: <https://github.com/GNS3/vpcs/archive/refs/tags/v0.8.3.tar.gz>
   47: - Pinned release: <https://github.com/GNS3/vpcs/releases/tag/v0.8.3>
   48: - License: BSD-2-Clause, as identified by the upstream repository
   49: 
   50: The archive redistributes the resulting binaries, not a moving branch checkout.
   51: The source URL and ref above are the corresponding source offer for these
   52: versions; the build recipe and compiler/link flags are recorded in
   53: `runtime/fetch-vpcs.sh`.
   54: 
   55: ### QEMU and the Apple Silicon archive ƒ?" what is and is not distributed
   56: 
   57: **No QEMU binary is contained in `iolbox-macos-arm64.tar.gz`.** The QEMU
   58: section further below covers the separate Windows launcher bundle, where we
   59: do redistribute QEMU binaries, and must not be read as a claim that the Mac
   60: artifact contains QEMU.
   61: 
   62: However, selecting the **`native-arm64`** profile *causes* QEMU to be
   63: installed on the user's machine, and that is worth stating plainly rather
   64: than leaving to the reader. `packaging/macos/guest/10-multiarch-native.sh`
   65: runs, inside the Lima guest:
   66: 
   67: ```sh
   68: apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
   69:     qemu-user-static binfmt-support libc6:amd64 libssl3t64:amd64
   70: ```
   71: 
   72: so that x86_64 IOL can be translated in-guest on a profile that deliberately
   73: has no Rosetta. `qemu-user-static` is GPL-licensed (QEMU is GPL-2.0, with
   74: components under LGPL-2.1 and other compatible licenses); `binfmt-support` is
   75: likewise GPL-licensed.
   76: 
   77: Boundary, stated explicitly:
   78: 
   79: - iolbox does **not** redistribute `qemu-user-static` or `binfmt-support`.
   80:   They are fetched at provisioning time by the guest's own `apt`, from
   81:   Debian's repositories, under Debian's packaging and copyright files ƒ?" the
   82:   same boundary this notice already draws for the guest image itself and for
   83:   every other guest package.
   84: - The distributor of those binaries is Debian, and Debian's corresponding
   85:   source is available from <https://sources.debian.org/> and via
   86:   `apt-get source qemu-user-static` on the guest. The exact versions selected
   87:   in qualification were `qemu-user-static 1:10.0.11+ds-0+deb13u1` and
   88:   `binfmt-support 2.2.2-7+b1`.
   89: - No QEMU or binfmt-support binary, source, or copyright file is embedded in
   90:   any iolbox artifact for macOS.
   91: 
   92: > **Open prerequisite, owner action required.** The M7 translator-selection
   93: > record sets `redistribution_review_required: true`, and no record shows
   94: > that review was performed (ledger row **P7-02**, `docs/macos-m7-result.md`).
   95: > The paragraphs above correct a notice that had become misleading; they are
   96: > **not** a substitute for that review and do not discharge it. It should be
   97: > closed before the first tag that ships the `native-arm64` profile.
   98: 
   99: ---
  100: 
  101: ## QEMU (Windows build) ƒ?" the `qemu` compatibility backend
  102: 
  103: The Windows launcher (`tools/iolab-launcher`) ships a trimmed copy of QEMU so the
  104: `qemu` backend (software-emulated TCG, see `docs/providers.md` and
  105: `runtime/qemu-compat.md`) works on any Windows machine with zero prerequisites.
  106: 
  107: ### Pinned source
  108: 
  109: | Field | Value |
  110: |---|---|
  111: | Upstream | Stefan Weil's official QEMU-for-Windows builds ƒ?" <https://qemu.weilnetz.de/w64/> |
  112: | File | `qemu-w64-setup-20260501.exe` |
  113: | Full URL | <https://qemu.weilnetz.de/w64/qemu-w64-setup-20260501.exe> |
  114: | QEMU version | 11.0.0 release build (reports `11.0.50 (v11.0.0-12631-g54e84cdc7a)`) |
  115: | Installer size | 190 MB (198,760,632 bytes) |
  116: | **SHA-256 (installer, verified by download)** | `a8b29572afb4c6ad024b7de129c81033e9fd191b9e054e3a52ea0bed24ac19ef` |
  117: 
  118: `qemu.weilnetz.de` is the canonical upstream-linked Windows build (referenced
  119: from qemu.org's download page). Note: recent installers are Authenticode-signed
  120: with an **expired certificate** ƒ?" Windows SmartScreen may warn on the installer.
  121: This does not affect the extracted binaries we redistribute (we extract, we do
  122: not run the installer on user machines).
  123: 
  124: ### How the redistributable is produced (extraction, not install)
  125: 
  126: The upstream `.exe` is an NSIS installer. We do **not** run it on user machines;
  127: we extract it once and ship a trimmed tree:
  128: 
  129: ```sh
  130: # 1. verify the pinned installer
  131: sha256sum qemu-w64-setup-20260501.exe
  132: #   -> a8b29572afb4c6ad024b7de129c81033e9fd191b9e054e3a52ea0bed24ac19ef
  133: 
  134: # 2. extract with 7-Zip (NSIS archive)
  135: "C:\Program Files\7-Zip\7z.exe" x -oqemu-extract qemu-w64-setup-20260501.exe
  136: 
  137: # 3. trim to the headless x86_64 target:
  138: #    - keep  qemu-system-x86_64.exe  + ALL *.dll (the runtime DLL set)
  139: #    - keep  share/keymaps/  and the x86/i386 firmware blobs
  140: #            (bios*.bin, vgabios*.bin, kvmvapic.bin, linuxboot*/multiboot*/pvh,
  141: #             *-virtio.rom + pxe-*.rom, edk2-i386/x86_64 *.fd)
  142: #    - drop  the other 55 qemu-system-*.exe targets, share/doc, and the
  143: #            non-x86 firmware (openbios-*, edk2-aarch64/arm, dtb, ...)
  144: ```
  145: 
  146: Result: a `qemu/` directory of ~175 MB. Verified standalone on a clean box:
  147: `qemu-system-x86_64.exe -version` and `-accel help` (lists `tcg` + `whpx`) both
  148: run, so the DLL set is complete.
  149: 
  150: ### Layout shipped next to the launcher exe
  151: 
  152: ```
  153: iolbox-launcher.exe
  154: iolbox-disk.qcow2            (the runtime disk ƒ?" a separate release asset, see below)
  155: qemu/
  156:   qemu-system-x86_64.exe
  157:   *.dll                     (the runtime DLLs)
  158:   share/
  159:     keymaps/
  160:     bios*.bin, vgabios*.bin, kvmvapic.bin, linuxboot*.bin, ...
  161: ```
  162: 
  163: The launcher looks for `qemu/qemu-system-x86_64.exe` and `iolbox-disk.qcow2`
  164: relative to its own exe (`--qemu` / `--disk` override for dev). QEMU resolves its
  165: BIOS/keymap data from the `share/` dir next to its exe automatically.
  166: 
  167: The `qemu/` directory and `*.qcow2` are **git-ignored** (see
  168: `tools/iolab-launcher/.gitignore`) ƒ?" they are release-time assets staged into the
  169: bundle, never committed to the repo.
  170: 
  171: ### License / GPL compliance
  172: 
  173: QEMU is licensed under the **GNU GPL v2** (with some components under LGPL v2.1
  174: and other compatible licenses). We redistribute unmodified upstream binaries.
  175: 
  176: - The upstream binaries carry their license texts (`COPYING`, `COPYING.LIB`) in
  177:   the installer; include a copy of `COPYING`/`COPYING.LIB` in the shipped `qemu/`
  178:   directory (or link to them from the release notes) when assembling a release.
  179: - **Written offer for source:** the corresponding source for this exact build is
  180:   published by the upstream packager at the QEMU source page,
  181:   <https://www.qemu.org/download/#source> (release 11.0.0), mirrored from
  182:   <https://qemu.weilnetz.de/>. iolbox distributes QEMU **unmodified**; the source
  183:   offer therefore points at upstream. Include this URL in the release notes /
  184:   About page alongside the version above so the offer travels with the binary.
  185: 
  186: ### The iolbox runtime disk (`iolbox-disk.qcow2`)
  187: 
  188: Not third-party ƒ?" it is built from `runtime/` (Debian-slim rootfs + the iolbox
  189: supervisor) by `runtime/pack-qemu.sh`. It contains **no Cisco software**; IOL
  190: images are supplied by the user at runtime via the GUI. Debian's own components
  191: inside the rootfs are under their respective licenses (Debian is DFSG-free);
  192: this is the same rootfs the WSL2 and VMware artifacts ship, already covered by
  193: the runtime build.
FILE: packaging/macos/guest/10-multiarch-native.sh [1-260]
    1: #!/usr/bin/env bash
    2: # 10-multiarch-native.sh ƒ?" configure the native-arm64 guest's translator and
    3: # amd64 runtime for the still-x86_64-only IOL device-image binary.
    4: #
    5: # "native-arm64" means the supervisor/vpcs/toollaunch userspace stack itself
    6: # is a real arm64 build (see runtime/pack-native.sh --arch arm64 and
    7: # docs/m7-phase4-file-mapping.md). It does NOT mean every executable in the
    8: # guest is arm64: the owner's IOL device-image binary is x86_64-only, and
    9: # Phase 3 (docs/macos-m7-phase3-execution-plan.md) measured and selected
   10: # qemu-user as the sole correctness-eligible in-guest translator for that one
   11: # binary. This step installs and registers that translator, plus the amd64
   12: # runtime libraries qemu-user's binfmt handler needs to resolve the IOL
   13: # binary's own dynamic dependencies ƒ?" the same amd64 libc6/libssl set the
   14: # Rosetta path installs via 10-multiarch-debian.sh, for the same reason.
   15: #
   16: # In order, this step:
   17: #   1. proves the guest is Debian trixie (the native-arm64 profile's pinned
   18: #      suite; see packaging/macos/lima/profiles.env);
   19: #   2. installs qemu-user-static and binfmt-support, and confirms Debian's
   20: #      packaging registered the qemu-x86_64 binfmt handler;
   21: #   3. installs the same amd64 libc6/libssl runtime set 10-multiarch-debian.sh
   22: #      installs, using the identical deb822/legacy source handling; and
   23: #   4. asserts the foreign architecture, the qemu-x86_64 handler, and the
   24: #      x86-64 loader/libc/libssl objects.
   25: set -euo pipefail
   26: 
   27: SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
   28: # shellcheck source=lib.sh
   29: . "$SCRIPT_DIR/lib.sh"
   30: 
   31: DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE="${DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE:-/etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources}"
   32: LEGACY_SOURCES_FILE="${LEGACY_SOURCES_FILE:-/etc/apt/sources.list}"
   33: IOLBOX_QEMU_X86_64_BINFMT="${IOLBOX_QEMU_X86_64_BINFMT:-/proc/sys/fs/binfmt_misc/qemu-x86_64}"
   34: 
   35: usage() {
   36:     cat <<EOF
   37: Usage: $0 [--verify]
   38: 
   39:   --verify    assert the native-arm64 translator/multiarch end state without
   40:               changing files or invoking apt.
   41:   -h, --help  show this help.
   42: EOF
   43: }
   44: 
   45: guest_codename() {
   46:     local distro_id='' codename=''
   47: 
   48:     [ -r /etc/os-release ] || die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_PREFLIGHT" \
   49:         'Debian identity assertion: /etc/os-release is missing'
   50:     # shellcheck disable=SC1091
   51:     . /etc/os-release
   52:     distro_id="${ID:-}"
   53:     codename="${VERSION_CODENAME:-}"
   54:     [ "$distro_id" = debian ] || die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_PREFLIGHT" \
   55:         "Debian identity assertion: expected ID=debian, detected '${distro_id:-unknown}'"
   56:     case "$codename" in
   57:         trixie) printf '%s\n' "$codename" ;;
   58:         *) die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_PREFLIGHT" \
   59:             "Debian identity assertion: expected VERSION_CODENAME=trixie (native-arm64 pins the same image as debian13), detected '${codename:-unknown}'" ;;
   60:     esac
   61: }
   62: 
   63: source_layout() {
   64:     if [ -f "$DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE" ]; then
   65:         printf 'deb822\n'
   66:     elif [ -f "$LEGACY_SOURCES_FILE" ]; then
   67:         printf 'legacy\n'
   68:     else
   69:         die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_PREFLIGHT" \
   70:             "Debian apt source assertion: neither $DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE nor $LEGACY_SOURCES_FILE exists"
   71:     fi
   72: }
   73: 
   74: deb822_needs_amd64() {
   75:     local line arch_list restricted=0
   76: 
   77:     while IFS= read -r line || [ -n "$line" ]; do
   78:         if [[ "$line" =~ ^[[:space:]]*Architectures:[[:space:]]*(.*)$ ]]; then
   79:             restricted=1
   80:             arch_list="${BASH_REMATCH[1]}"
   81:             if [[ " $arch_list " != *' amd64 '* ]]; then
   82:                 return 0
   83:             fi
   84:         fi
   85:     done < "$DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE"
   86:     [ "$restricted" -eq 1 ] && return 1
   87:     return 1
   88: }
   89: 
   90: enable_deb822_amd64() {
   91:     local backup tmp line arch_list prefix changed=0
   92: 
   93:     if ! deb822_needs_amd64; then
   94:         return 0
   95:     fi
   96:     backup="${DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE}.iolbox-orig"
   97:     if [ ! -e "$backup" ]; then
   98:         cp -- "$DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE" "$backup" || die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_PREFLIGHT" \
   99:             "could not back up Debian deb822 sources: $DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE"
  100:     fi
  101:     tmp="$(mktemp "${DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE}.iolbox-tmp.XXXXXX")" || \
  102:         die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_PREFLIGHT" 'could not create a Debian sources temporary file'
  103:     while IFS= read -r line || [ -n "$line" ]; do
  104:         if [[ "$line" =~ ^([[:space:]]*)Architectures:[[:space:]]*(.*)$ ]]; then
  105:             prefix="${BASH_REMATCH[1]}"
  106:             arch_list="${BASH_REMATCH[2]}"
  107:             if [[ " $arch_list " != *' amd64 '* ]]; then
  108:                 printf '%sArchitectures: %s amd64\n' "$prefix" "$arch_list" >> "$tmp"
  109:                 changed=1
  110:             else
  111:                 printf '%s\n' "$line" >> "$tmp"
  112:             fi
  113:         else
  114:             printf '%s\n' "$line" >> "$tmp"
  115:         fi
  116:     done < "$DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE"
  117:     if [ "$changed" -eq 1 ]; then
  118:         mv -f -- "$tmp" "$DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE" || die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_PREFLIGHT" \
  119:             "could not install amended Debian sources: $DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE"
  120:     else
  121:         rm -f -- "$tmp"
  122:     fi
  123: }
  124: 
  125: prepare_sources() {
  126:     local layout
  127: 
  128:     layout="$(source_layout)"
  129:     case "$layout" in
  130:         deb822)
  131:             enable_deb822_amd64
  132:             log "using Debian deb822 sources: $DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE; deb.debian.org serves both amd64 and arm64, so no mirror rewrite is needed"
  133:             ;;
  134:         legacy)
  135:             log "using legacy Debian one-line sources: $LEGACY_SOURCES_FILE; no source rewriting is needed"
  136:             ;;
  137:     esac
  138: }
  139: 
  140: verify_sources() {
  141:     local layout line arch_list
  142: 
  143:     layout="$(source_layout)"
  144:     if [ "$layout" = deb822 ]; then
  145:         while IFS= read -r line || [ -n "$line" ]; do
  146:             if [[ "$line" =~ ^[[:space:]]*Architectures:[[:space:]]*(.*)$ ]]; then
  147:                 arch_list="${BASH_REMATCH[1]}"
  148:                 [[ " $arch_list " == *' amd64 '* ]] || die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_VERIFY" \
  149:                     "source assertion: restrictive Architectures field omits amd64 in $DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE"
  150:             fi
  151:         done < "$DEBIAN_SOURCES_FILE"
  152:     fi
  153: }
  154: 
  155: find_amd64_libc() {
  156:     dpkg-query -L libc6:amd64 2>/dev/null | awk '/\/libc\.so\.6$/ { print; exit }'
  157: }
  158: 
  159: find_amd64_libssl() {
  160:     dpkg-query -L libssl3t64:amd64 2>/dev/null | awk '/\/libssl\.so\.[0-9]+$/ { print; exit }'
  161: }
  162: 
  163: package_is_installed() {
  164:     local package="$1"
  165:     [ "$(dpkg-query -W -f='${Architecture} ${Status}\n' "$package" 2>/dev/null || true)" = \
  166:         "${package##*:} install ok installed" ]
  167: }
  168: 
  169: package_is_installed_native() {
  170:     local package="$1"
  171:     [ "$(dpkg-query -W -f='${Status}\n' "$package" 2>/dev/null || true)" = 'install ok installed' ]
  172: }
  173: 
  174: qemu_x86_64_binfmt_state() {
  175:     if [ -r "$IOLBOX_QEMU_X86_64_BINFMT" ]; then
  176:         printf 'registered: %s' "$(tr '\n' ' ' < "$IOLBOX_QEMU_X86_64_BINFMT")"
  177:     else
  178:         printf 'absent: %s is unreadable or missing' "$IOLBOX_QEMU_X86_64_BINFMT"
  179:     fi
  180: }
  181: 
  182: verify_runtime() {
  183:     local exit_code="$1" libc_path ssl_path foreign_architectures
  184: 
  185:     package_is_installed_native qemu-user-static || die "$exit_code" \
  186:         'package assertion: qemu-user-static is not installed'
  187:     package_is_installed_native binfmt-support || die "$exit_code" \
  188:         'package assertion: binfmt-support is not installed'
  189:     if [ ! -r "$IOLBOX_QEMU_X86_64_BINFMT" ] || ! grep -q '^enabled' "$IOLBOX_QEMU_X86_64_BINFMT"; then
  190:         die "$exit_code" \
  191:             "translator assertion: qemu-x86_64 binfmt handler is not registered/enabled ($(qemu_x86_64_binfmt_state))"
  192:     fi
  193: 
  194:     package_is_installed libc6:amd64 || die "$exit_code" \
  195:         'package assertion: libc6:amd64 is not installed'
  196:     package_is_installed libssl3t64:amd64 || die "$exit_code" \
  197:         'package assertion: libssl3t64:amd64 is not installed'
  198:     foreign_architectures="$(dpkg --print-foreign-architectures 2>/dev/null || true)"
  199:     if ! text_contains_exact_line "$foreign_architectures" amd64; then
  200:         die "$exit_code" \
  201:             'architecture assertion: dpkg --print-foreign-architectures does not contain amd64'
  202:     fi
  203:     libc_path="$(find_amd64_libc || true)"
  204:     [ -n "$libc_path" ] || die "$exit_code" \
  205:         'ELF assertion: dpkg has no libc6:amd64 libc.so.6 path'
  206:     ssl_path="$(find_amd64_libssl || true)"
  207:     [ -n "$ssl_path" ] || die "$exit_code" \
  208:         'ELF assertion: dpkg has no libssl3t64:amd64 libssl.so path'
  209:     assert_amd64_elf "$libc_path"
  210:     assert_amd64_elf "$ssl_path"
  211: }
  212: 
  213: run_provision() {
  214:     local rc codename
  215: 
  216:     codename="$(guest_codename)"
  217:     prepare_sources
  218: 
  219:     if dpkg --add-architecture amd64; then
  220:         :
  221:     else
  222:         rc=$?
  223:         die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_APT" "command failed (exit $rc): dpkg --add-architecture amd64"
  224:     fi
  225:     if DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get update; then
  226:         :
  227:     else
  228:         rc=$?
  229:         die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_APT" \
  230:             "command failed (exit $rc): DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get update"
  231:     fi
  232:     if DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
  233:         qemu-user-static binfmt-support libc6:amd64 libssl3t64:amd64; then
  234:         :
  235:     else
  236:         rc=$?
  237:         die "$IOLBOX_EXIT_APT" \
  238:             "command failed (exit $rc): DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends qemu-user-static binfmt-support libc6:amd64 libssl3t64:amd64"
  239:     fi
  240:     # Debian's qemu-user-static postinst normally registers binfmt handlers
  241:     # via update-binfmts automatically; make it explicit and idempotent so a
  242:     # provisioning re-run cannot silently skip it.
  243:     if have update-binfmts; then
  244:         update-binfmts --enable qemu-x86_64 2>/dev/null || true
  245:     fi
  246:     verify_runtime "$IOLBOX_EXIT_APT"
  247:     log "native-arm64 translator (qemu-user) and amd64 runtime are installed and verified: $codename"
  248: }
  249: 
  250: verify_end_state() {
  251:     verify_sources
  252:     verify_runtime "$IOLBOX_EXIT_VERIFY"
  253: }
  254: 
  255: main() {
  256:     local verify=0
  257: 
  258:     while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  259:         case "$1" in
  260:             --verify) verify=1; shift ;;
FILE: runtime/pack-native.sh [1-280]
    1: #!/usr/bin/env bash
    2: # pack-native.sh ƒ?" package iolbox as a standalone installer tarball for ANY
    3: # systemd glibc Linux server (bare metal, cloud VM, on-prem hypervisor guest
    4: # ƒ?" not the WSL2/VMware appliance rootfs the other pack-* scripts build, and
    5: # not a macOS Lima/VZ guest ƒ?" the M7 native-arm64 profile uses this same
    6: # packager with --arch arm64, then the macOS launcher's install.sh flow runs
    7: # it inside the guest). See docs/providers.md's `remote` provider and
    8: # runtime/files/native/README.txt for what ships inside.
    9: #
   10: # Unlike pack-wsl.sh/pack-vmware.sh, this does NOT consume the debootstrap
   11: # rootfs from build-rootfs.sh ƒ?" a native install runs on the OPERATOR's own
   12: # distro, whatever it already has, so this script only needs the two
   13: # binaries (supervisor, vpcs) plus the support files under
   14: # runtime/files/{,native/}. No root required to run this script.
   15: #
   16: # Output: runtime/build/iolbox-server-<version>.tar.gz (amd64, historical
   17: # name) or runtime/build/iolbox-server-<version>-linux-<arch>.tar.gz when
   18: # --arch is passed explicitly.
   19: set -euo pipefail
   20: 
   21: SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
   22: BUILD_DIR="${IOLBOX_BUILD_DIR:-$SCRIPT_DIR/build}"
   23: FILES_DIR="$SCRIPT_DIR/files"
   24: NATIVE_DIR="$FILES_DIR/native"
   25: 
   26: VERSION="dev"
   27: TARGET_ARCH="amd64"
   28: ARCH_EXPLICIT=0
   29: VALIDATE_ONLY=0
   30: # Same default search order build-rootfs.sh uses for the supervisor binary;
   31: # see that script's SUPERVISOR_BIN comment (matches PLAN.md repo layout +
   32: # .gitignore's /supervisor/bin/). Preferred over the rootfs copy when both
   33: # exist, per this script's brief ("prefer the explicit --supervisor-bin
   34: # flag like the other pack scripts" ƒ?" --supervisor-bin always wins).
   35: # These are recomputed after flag parsing once TARGET_ARCH is final (see
   36: # below) so --arch arm64 picks up supervisor-linux-arm64 instead of the
   37: # amd64 default.
   38: SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_1="$SCRIPT_DIR/../supervisor/bin/supervisor-linux-$TARGET_ARCH"
   39: SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_2="$BUILD_DIR/rootfs/opt/iolbox/supervisor"
   40: SUPERVISOR_BIN=""
   41: VPCS_BIN_DEFAULT="$BUILD_DIR/vpcs/vpcs"     # fetch-vpcs.sh's output path
   42: VPCS_BIN=""
   43: # Source, not a prebuilt binary: unlike vpcs (fetched) and supervisor (built by
   44: # build-release.sh), iolbox-toollaunch is trivial to cross-compile here with
   45: # CGO disabled, matching how runtime/build-rootfs.sh builds it (see that
   46: # script's `go build -trimpath` invocation for TOOLLAUNCH_BIN).
   47: TOOLLAUNCH_SRC_DEFAULT="$SCRIPT_DIR/../tools/iolbox-toollaunch"
   48: TOOLLAUNCH_SRC=""
   49: TOOLLAUNCH_BIN=""
   50: # Learning-tool packs (see docs/ for the P2/P3 plans). Each simple pack is a
   51: # single static Go binary that is both the pack's AF_UNIX GUI and its
   52: # lab-facing service; "pc" is the built-in netprobe pack PC/VPCS nodes require
   53: # (see supervisor/internal/server/toolpacks.go). secbench additionally ships a
   54: # directory of standalone attack binaries under tools/secbench-attacks-go.
   55: # Skippable with --no-packs for callers that only need supervisor/vpcs (e.g. a
   56: # quick IOL-only smoke build) and don't want the extra build time. Every pack
   57: # and the secbench attack binaries are cross-compiled for TARGET_ARCH, same as
   58: # supervisor/toollaunch ƒ?" a native-arm64 package must not silently ship amd64
   59: # pack binaries.
   60: SIMPLE_PACKS="aaa webserver httpclient syslog netsvc pc"
   61: SECBENCH_ATTACKS_SRC_DEFAULT="$SCRIPT_DIR/../tools/secbench-attacks-go"
   62: SKIP_PACKS=0
   63: OUT_DIR="$BUILD_DIR"
   64: 
   65: usage() {
   66:     cat <<EOF
   67: Usage: $0 [options]
   68: 
   69:   --version X.Y.Z         Version string embedded in the output filename and
   70:                            the top-level directory inside the tarball
   71:                            (default: $VERSION)
   72:   --arch ARCH              Payload architecture: amd64 (default) or arm64.
   73:                            No-argument amd64 keeps the historical package
   74:                            name/layout; an explicit --arch (including
   75:                            --arch amd64) suffixes the package name with
   76:                            -linux-<arch> and writes manifest.env.
   77:   --supervisor-bin PATH   Path to the built Go supervisor binary. Build it
   78:                            with the repo's build-release.sh (the GUI bundle
   79:                            must be embedded ƒ?" a plain 'go build' ships a
   80:                            placeholder GUI). Default: first of
   81:                              $SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_1
   82:                              $SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_2
   83:                            that exists.
   84:   --vpcs-bin PATH          Path to a prebuilt linux/\$TARGET_ARCH vpcs binary.
   85:                            Default: $VPCS_BIN_DEFAULT (run ./fetch-vpcs.sh
   86:                            first, or drop a binary there by hand)
   87:   --toollaunch-bin PATH    Path to a prebuilt linux/\$TARGET_ARCH
   88:                            iolbox-toollaunch binary. Default: cross-compiled
   89:                            on the fly from $TOOLLAUNCH_SRC_DEFAULT (requires
   90:                            'go' on PATH).
   91:   --no-packs               Skip building/staging the learning-tool packs
   92:                            (aaa/webserver/httpclient/syslog/netsvc/pc/secbench).
   93:                            PC/VPCS nodes will not work without them.
   94:   --build-dir DIR          Output root (default: $BUILD_DIR)
   95:   --out DIR                Where to write the tarball (default: --build-dir)
   96:   --validate-only          Validate supplied/resolved ELF architectures
   97:                            (supervisor, vpcs, toollaunch), then exit 0
   98:                            without staging or packing anything.
   99:   -h, --help               This help
  100: 
  101: Output: <out>/iolbox-server-<version>[-linux-<arch>].tar.gz
  102: EOF
  103: }
  104: 
  105: while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  106:     case "$1" in
  107:         --version) VERSION="$2"; shift 2 ;;
  108:         --arch) TARGET_ARCH="$2"; ARCH_EXPLICIT=1; shift 2 ;;
  109:         --arch=*) TARGET_ARCH="${1#*=}"; ARCH_EXPLICIT=1; shift ;;
  110:         --supervisor-bin) SUPERVISOR_BIN="$2"; shift 2 ;;
  111:         --vpcs-bin) VPCS_BIN="$2"; shift 2 ;;
  112:         --toollaunch-bin) TOOLLAUNCH_BIN="$2"; shift 2 ;;
  113:         --no-packs) SKIP_PACKS=1; shift ;;
  114:         --build-dir) BUILD_DIR="$2"; OUT_DIR="$BUILD_DIR"; shift 2 ;;
  115:         --out) OUT_DIR="$2"; shift 2 ;;
  116:         --validate-only) VALIDATE_ONLY=1; shift ;;
  117:         -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
  118:         *) echo "unknown option: $1" >&2; usage; exit 1 ;;
  119:     esac
  120: done
  121: 
  122: case "$TARGET_ARCH" in
  123:     amd64|arm64) ;;
  124:     *) echo "pack-native: --arch must be amd64 or arm64, got '$TARGET_ARCH'" >&2; exit 1 ;;
  125: esac
  126: 
  127: # Normalize to absolute paths now that --build-dir/--out are final. Several
  128: # steps below (the tool-pack build loop in particular) build inside a `cd`'d
  129: # subshell; a relative BUILD_DIR/OUT_DIR would resolve against that subshell's
  130: # cwd instead of the caller's, silently writing packs to the wrong place and
  131: # leaving PACK_STAGE never created for the `install` calls that follow.
  132: mkdir -p "$BUILD_DIR" "$OUT_DIR"
  133: BUILD_DIR="$(cd "$BUILD_DIR" && pwd)"
  134: OUT_DIR="$(cd "$OUT_DIR" && pwd)"
  135: 
  136: # Recompute architecture-sensitive defaults after all flags have been parsed
  137: # and BUILD_DIR is absolute; this preserves the no-argument amd64 paths while
  138: # making --arch arm64 select the matching supervisor payload.
  139: SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_1="$SCRIPT_DIR/../supervisor/bin/supervisor-linux-$TARGET_ARCH"
  140: SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_2="$BUILD_DIR/rootfs/opt/iolbox/supervisor"
  141: VPCS_BIN_DEFAULT="$BUILD_DIR/vpcs/vpcs"
  142: 
  143: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  144: # Resolve binary sources
  145: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  146: if [ -z "$SUPERVISOR_BIN" ]; then
  147:     if [ -f "$SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_1" ]; then
  148:         SUPERVISOR_BIN="$SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_1"
  149:     elif [ -f "$SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_2" ]; then
  150:         SUPERVISOR_BIN="$SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_2"
  151:     fi
  152: fi
  153: 
  154: if [ -z "$SUPERVISOR_BIN" ] || [ ! -f "$SUPERVISOR_BIN" ]; then
  155:     cat >&2 <<EOF
  156: pack-native: supervisor binary not found. Checked:
  157:   $SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_1
  158:   $SUPERVISOR_BIN_DEFAULT_2
  159: 
  160: Build it first (from the repo root):
  161:   bash build-release.sh    # -> supervisor/bin/supervisor-linux-$TARGET_ARCH
  162:                             # (embeds the GUI bundle; plain 'go build' does not)
  163: 
  164: ...or pass --supervisor-bin /path/to/binary.
  165: EOF
  166:     exit 1
  167: fi
  168: 
  169: if [ -z "$VPCS_BIN" ]; then
  170:     VPCS_BIN="$VPCS_BIN_DEFAULT"
  171: fi
  172: 
  173: # A Windows/Git-Bash cross-build workspace may not preserve the POSIX execute
  174: # bit on a transferred ELF. The archive staging below applies 0755, while
  175: # require_elf_arch immediately after this check proves the input is an ELF of
  176: # the requested architecture, so require a regular file here, not host-mode
  177: # metadata that Windows cannot represent faithfully.
  178: if [ ! -f "$VPCS_BIN" ]; then
  179:     cat >&2 <<EOF
  180: pack-native: vpcs binary not found or not a regular file at:
  181:   $VPCS_BIN
  182: 
  183: Run ./fetch-vpcs.sh first (needs network access), or drop a prebuilt
  184: linux/$TARGET_ARCH vpcs binary at that path by hand, or pass --vpcs-bin PATH.
  185: EOF
  186:     exit 1
  187: fi
  188: 
  189: if [ -z "$TOOLLAUNCH_BIN" ]; then
  190:     if [ -z "$TOOLLAUNCH_SRC" ]; then
  191:         TOOLLAUNCH_SRC="$TOOLLAUNCH_SRC_DEFAULT"
  192:     fi
  193:     if [ ! -d "$TOOLLAUNCH_SRC" ]; then
  194:         cat >&2 <<EOF
  195: pack-native: iolbox-toollaunch source not found at:
  196:   $TOOLLAUNCH_SRC
  197: 
  198: Pass --toollaunch-bin PATH to use a prebuilt linux/$TARGET_ARCH binary instead.
  199: EOF
  200:         exit 1
  201:     fi
  202:     command -v go >/dev/null 2>&1 || {
  203:         cat >&2 <<EOF
  204: pack-native: 'go' is not on PATH, needed to build iolbox-toollaunch from
  205:   $TOOLLAUNCH_SRC
  206: 
  207: Install Go, or pass --toollaunch-bin PATH to use a prebuilt linux/$TARGET_ARCH
  208: binary instead.
  209: EOF
  210:         exit 1
  211:     }
  212:     TOOLLAUNCH_BIN="$BUILD_DIR/iolbox-toollaunch-$TARGET_ARCH"
  213:     echo "== pack-native: building iolbox-toollaunch from $TOOLLAUNCH_SRC (linux/$TARGET_ARCH) =="
  214:     ( cd "$TOOLLAUNCH_SRC" && GOOS=linux GOARCH="$TARGET_ARCH" CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -o "$TOOLLAUNCH_BIN" . )
  215: fi
  216: 
  217: if [ ! -x "$TOOLLAUNCH_BIN" ] && [ ! -f "$TOOLLAUNCH_BIN" ]; then
  218:     echo "pack-native: iolbox-toollaunch binary not found at: $TOOLLAUNCH_BIN" >&2
  219:     exit 1
  220: fi
  221: 
  222: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  223: # Fail-closed ELF architecture validation. A native package must never be
  224: # assembled with a binary that cannot execute on the requested TARGET_ARCH ƒ?"
  225: # this replaces the earlier amd64-only, warning-only 'file' probe with a hard
  226: # gate that understands both amd64 and arm64 ELF headers, using 'file' when
  227: # present and falling back to 'readelf -h'.
  228: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  229: require_elf_arch() {
  230:     local path="$1"
  231:     local expected="$2"
  232:     local label="$3"
  233:     local description
  234: 
  235:     if command -v file >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  236:         if ! description="$(file -b -- "$path" 2>&1)"; then
  237:             echo "$label: file failed while inspecting $path: $description" >&2
  238:             return 1
  239:         fi
  240:         case "$expected:$description" in
  241:             amd64:*"ELF 64-bit"*"x86-64"*) ;;
  242:             arm64:*"ELF 64-bit"*"ARM aarch64"*) ;;
  243:             arm64:*"ELF 64-bit"*"AArch64"*) ;;
  244:             *)
  245:                 echo "$label: $path is not a linux/$expected ELF: $description" >&2
  246:                 return 1
  247:                 ;;
  248:         esac
  249:         return 0
  250:     fi
  251: 
  252:     if command -v readelf >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  253:         if ! description="$(readelf -h "$path" 2>&1)"; then
  254:             echo "$label: readelf failed while inspecting $path: $description" >&2
  255:             return 1
  256:         fi
  257:         case "$expected:$description" in
  258:             amd64:*"Class:"*"ELF64"*"Machine:"*"X86-64"*) ;;
  259:             arm64:*"Class:"*"ELF64"*"Machine:"*"AArch64"*) ;;
  260:             *)
  261:                 echo "$label: $path is not a linux/$expected ELF (readelf header did not match)" >&2
  262:                 return 1
  263:                 ;;
  264:         esac
  265:         return 0
  266:     fi
  267: 
  268:     echo "$label: neither 'file' nor 'readelf' is available to verify $path is linux/$expected; refusing to assemble an unverified native package" >&2
  269:     return 1
  270: }
  271: 
  272: require_elf_arch "$SUPERVISOR_BIN" "$TARGET_ARCH" "pack-native"
  273: require_elf_arch "$VPCS_BIN" "$TARGET_ARCH" "pack-native"
  274: require_elf_arch "$TOOLLAUNCH_BIN" "$TARGET_ARCH" "pack-native"
  275: 
  276: if [ "$VALIDATE_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
  277:     echo "pack-native: architecture validation passed for linux/$TARGET_ARCH"
  278:     exit 0
  279: fi
  280: 
FILE: packaging/macos/pack-release.sh [1-260]
    1: #!/usr/bin/env bash
    2: # Build the unsigned Apple Silicon release archive from explicit inputs.
    3: #
    4: # This script deliberately has no CI-workspace discovery. The caller supplies
    5: # the Darwin launcher, BOTH exact payloads and their trusted digests, the
    6: # release/ref version, output path, and SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH.
    7: #
    8: # Two payloads, because the archive serves two execution profiles:
    9: #   --payload        the historical untagged amd64 tarball, run under Rosetta
   10: #                    by the debian13/jammy/debian12 profiles. Unchanged.
   11: #   --payload-arm64  the linux/arm64 tarball used by the native-arm64 profile.
   12: # The launcher picks between them from the resolved profile; see selectPayload
   13: # in tools/iolab-launcher/macos_lima.go.
   14: set -euo pipefail
   15: 
   16: SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
   17: REPO_ROOT="$(cd "$SCRIPT_DIR/../.." && pwd)"
   18: MANIFEST="$SCRIPT_DIR/release-manifest.txt"
   19: ARCHIVE_ROOT_NAME="iolbox-macos-arm64"
   20: 
   21: LAUNCHER=""
   22: PAYLOAD=""
   23: PAYLOAD_SHA256=""
   24: PAYLOAD_ARM64=""
   25: PAYLOAD_ARM64_SHA256=""
   26: VERSION=""
   27: OUTPUT=""
   28: SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=""
   29: 
   30: usage() {
   31:     cat <<'EOF'
   32: Usage: packaging/macos/pack-release.sh \
   33:   --launcher PATH --payload PATH --payload-sha256 SHA256 \
   34:   --payload-arm64 PATH --payload-arm64-sha256 SHA256 \
   35:   --version VERSION --output PATH --source-date-epoch EPOCH
   36: 
   37: All eight inputs are required.
   38: 
   39:   --payload / --payload-sha256              amd64 payload, run under Rosetta by
   40:                                             the debian13/jammy/debian12
   41:                                             profiles. Basename must be
   42:                                             iolbox-server-<version>.tar.gz
   43:   --payload-arm64 / --payload-arm64-sha256  linux/arm64 payload, used by the
   44:                                             native-arm64 profile. Basename must
   45:                                             be
   46:                                             iolbox-server-<version>-linux-arm64.tar.gz
   47: 
   48: Both payloads are REQUIRED. With the native profile assets in the archive, a
   49: qualifying host's `auto` selects native; an archive missing the arm64 payload
   50: would fail only AFTER the profile is locked in, with no fallback left.
   51: Requiring both makes that state unrepresentable.
   52: 
   53: Payloads and launcher are never discovered by searching a build directory; the
   54: caller must identify and authenticate them.
   55: EOF
   56: }
   57: 
   58: die() {
   59:     echo "pack-release: $*" >&2
   60:     exit 1
   61: }
   62: 
   63: while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
   64:     case "$1" in
   65:         --launcher) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--launcher needs a value"; LAUNCHER="$2"; shift 2 ;;
   66:         --payload) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--payload needs a value"; PAYLOAD="$2"; shift 2 ;;
   67:         --payload-sha256) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--payload-sha256 needs a value"; PAYLOAD_SHA256="$2"; shift 2 ;;
   68:         --payload-arm64) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--payload-arm64 needs a value"; PAYLOAD_ARM64="$2"; shift 2 ;;
   69:         --payload-arm64-sha256) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--payload-arm64-sha256 needs a value"; PAYLOAD_ARM64_SHA256="$2"; shift 2 ;;
   70:         --version) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--version needs a value"; VERSION="$2"; shift 2 ;;
   71:         --output) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--output needs a value"; OUTPUT="$2"; shift 2 ;;
   72:         --source-date-epoch) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--source-date-epoch needs a value"; SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH="$2"; shift 2 ;;
   73:         -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
   74:         *) die "unknown option: $1" ;;
   75:     esac
   76: done
   77: 
   78: [ -n "$LAUNCHER" ] || die "--launcher is required"
   79: [ -n "$PAYLOAD" ] || die "--payload is required"
   80: [ -n "$PAYLOAD_SHA256" ] || die "--payload-sha256 is required"
   81: [ -n "$PAYLOAD_ARM64" ] || die "--payload-arm64 is required"
   82: [ -n "$PAYLOAD_ARM64_SHA256" ] || die "--payload-arm64-sha256 is required"
   83: [ -n "$VERSION" ] || die "--version is required"
   84: [ -n "$OUTPUT" ] || die "--output is required"
   85: [ -n "$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" ] || die "--source-date-epoch is required"
   86: 
   87: [[ "$PAYLOAD_SHA256" =~ ^[0-9A-Fa-f]{64}$ ]] || die "--payload-sha256 must be 64 hexadecimal characters"
   88: [[ "$PAYLOAD_ARM64_SHA256" =~ ^[0-9A-Fa-f]{64}$ ]] || die "--payload-arm64-sha256 must be 64 hexadecimal characters"
   89: [[ "$VERSION" =~ ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$ ]] || die "version contains unsupported filename characters: $VERSION"
   90: [[ "$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || die "--source-date-epoch must be a non-negative integer"
   91: 
   92: LAUNCHER="$(cd "$(dirname "$LAUNCHER")" && pwd)/$(basename "$LAUNCHER")"
   93: PAYLOAD="$(cd "$(dirname "$PAYLOAD")" && pwd)/$(basename "$PAYLOAD")"
   94: PAYLOAD_ARM64="$(cd "$(dirname "$PAYLOAD_ARM64")" && pwd)/$(basename "$PAYLOAD_ARM64")"
   95: OUTPUT="$(cd "$(dirname "$OUTPUT")" 2>/dev/null || { mkdir -p "$(dirname "$OUTPUT")"; cd "$(dirname "$OUTPUT")"; } && pwd)/$(basename "$OUTPUT")"
   96: 
   97: [ -f "$LAUNCHER" ] && [ ! -L "$LAUNCHER" ] || die "launcher must be a regular non-symlink file: $LAUNCHER"
   98: [ -f "$PAYLOAD" ] && [ ! -L "$PAYLOAD" ] || die "payload must be a regular non-symlink file: $PAYLOAD"
   99: [ -f "$PAYLOAD_ARM64" ] && [ ! -L "$PAYLOAD_ARM64" ] || die "arm64 payload must be a regular non-symlink file: $PAYLOAD_ARM64"
  100: command -v file >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "file is required to verify the Darwin launcher"
  101: command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "sha256sum is required on the Ubuntu packer"
  102: command -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "GNU tar is required"
  103: command -v gzip >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "gzip is required"
  104: tar --version | grep -F 'GNU tar' >/dev/null || die "tar is not GNU tar"
  105: 
  106: EXPECTED_PAYLOAD="iolbox-server-${VERSION}.tar.gz"
  107: EXPECTED_PAYLOAD_ARM64="iolbox-server-${VERSION}-linux-arm64.tar.gz"
  108: [ "$(basename "$PAYLOAD")" = "$EXPECTED_PAYLOAD" ] || die "payload basename is $(basename "$PAYLOAD"), expected $EXPECTED_PAYLOAD"
  109: [ "$(basename "$PAYLOAD_ARM64")" = "$EXPECTED_PAYLOAD_ARM64" ] || die "arm64 payload basename is $(basename "$PAYLOAD_ARM64"), expected $EXPECTED_PAYLOAD_ARM64"
  110: [ "$(basename "$OUTPUT")" = "${ARCHIVE_ROOT_NAME}.tar.gz" ] || die "output must be named ${ARCHIVE_ROOT_NAME}.tar.gz"
  111: 
  112: LAUNCHER_FILE="$(file -b "$LAUNCHER")"
  113: case "$LAUNCHER_FILE" in
  114:     *"Mach-O 64-bit"*"arm64"*) ;;
  115:     *) die "launcher is not a Mach-O arm64 executable: $LAUNCHER_FILE" ;;
  116: esac
  117: 
  118: ACTUAL_PAYLOAD="$(sha256sum "$PAYLOAD" | awk '{print tolower($1)}')"
  119: [ "$ACTUAL_PAYLOAD" = "$(printf '%s' "$PAYLOAD_SHA256" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')" ] || die "payload hash does not match trusted --payload-sha256 (actual $ACTUAL_PAYLOAD)"
  120: ACTUAL_PAYLOAD_ARM64="$(sha256sum "$PAYLOAD_ARM64" | awk '{print tolower($1)}')"
  121: [ "$ACTUAL_PAYLOAD_ARM64" = "$(printf '%s' "$PAYLOAD_ARM64_SHA256" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')" ] || die "arm64 payload hash does not match trusted --payload-arm64-sha256 (actual $ACTUAL_PAYLOAD_ARM64)"
  122: 
  123: [ -f "$MANIFEST" ] && [ ! -L "$MANIFEST" ] || die "release manifest is missing or is a symlink: $MANIFEST"
  124: 
  125: declare -a MANIFEST_SOURCES=()
  126: declare -a MANIFEST_DESTS=()
  127: while IFS='|' read -r source dest extra || [ -n "${source:-}" ]; do
  128:     case "${source:-}" in
  129:         ""|\#*) continue ;;
  130:     esac
  131:     [ -n "${dest:-}" ] && [ -z "${extra:-}" ] || die "manifest line must be source|destination: $source|$dest${extra:+|$extra}"
  132:     case "$source" in
  133:         /*|../*|*/../*|.|*/./*) die "manifest source escapes repository: $source" ;;
  134:     esac
  135:     case "$dest" in
  136:         ""|/*|../*|*/../*|.|*/./*) die "manifest destination is unsafe: $dest" ;;
  137:     esac
  138:     source_path="$REPO_ROOT/$source"
  139:     [ -f "$source_path" ] && [ ! -L "$source_path" ] || die "manifest source is not a regular non-symlink file: $source"
  140:     for existing in "${MANIFEST_DESTS[@]}"; do
  141:         [ "$existing" != "$dest" ] || die "manifest destination appears more than once: $dest"
  142:     done
  143:     MANIFEST_SOURCES+=("$source")
  144:     MANIFEST_DESTS+=("$dest")
  145: done < "$MANIFEST"
  146: 
  147: [ "${#MANIFEST_SOURCES[@]}" -eq 24 ] || die "manifest has ${#MANIFEST_SOURCES[@]} entries, expected 24"
  148: 
  149: for required_dest in \
  150:     README.md LICENSE notices/THIRD_PARTY.md \
